1330                             ; add32:  32-bit addition.  scratcha += scratchb
1331                             ; Usage:
1332                             ;      call add32
1333                             ;
1334                             ; Input:
1335                             ;      32-bits of scratchb
1336                             ;      32-bits of scratcha
1337                             ;
1338                             ; Output:
1339                             ;      32-bits of scratcha, the carry bit contains any overflow
1340                             ;
1341                             ; Returns:
1342                             ;      The carry bit has any overflow generated from the addition
1343                             ;
1344                             ; Uses:
1345                             ;      scratchb is destroyed.
1346                             ;
1347                             ; Desc:
1348                             ;      This operation is surprisingly difficult with the NCR instruction
1349                             ;      set and probably represents a major departure between NCR's intended
1350                             ;      use of the chip and Intel's requirements.
1351                             ;
1352                             ; Algorithm:
1353                             ;      Uses the "register to register move" instruction (an 8-bit move)
1354                             ;      which includes an obscure ability to add an 8-bit value.  The 8-bit
1355                             ;      value must be a constant coded into the "move" instruction.  32-bit
1356                             ;      addition requires 4 additions plus dealing with byte to byte carrys.
1357                             ;
1358                             ;      Move the 4 bytes of scratchb into the 4 instructions where +XXX
1359                             ;      appears.  +XXX is a place holder to (a) persuade the assembler to
1360                             ;      generate the right opcode and (b) provide a visual pattern in a hex
1361                             ;      dump to be sure the right place is modified.
1362                             ;
1363                             ;      Complication!  The move memory instruction is the only mechanism the
1364                             ;      NCR chip provides usable for modifying instructions.  Unfortunately,
1365                             ;      it demands the source and destination be the same number of bytes
1366                             ;      past the last 4-byte boundary.  That is, the source and destination
1367                             ;      address must have the same least significant 2 bits.  (If they are
1368                             ;      not, an "illegal instruction exception occurs.)  As the destination
1369                             ;      is always byte 1 of an instruction, scratchb1 is the only register
1370                             ;      aligned correctly.
1371                             
